## Abstract

The exotic electronic states in the charge loop current (cLC) phase, in which the
permanent charge current breaks the time-reversal symmetry, have been attracting
increasing attention in recently discovered kagome metals AV$_3$Sb$_5$ (A = Cs, Rb, K).
The cLC state is sensitively controlled by a small magnetic field and by tiny uniaxial
strain, and many experiments indicate it is sensitive to a small number of impurities.
We analyze the giant unit-cell (up to 1200 sites) kagome lattice model with a single
impurity potential. The loop current is strongly suppressed within the current
correlation length $\xi_J$ centered on the impurity, where $\xi_J$ increases as the
cLC order parameter $\eta$ decreases (cLC: $\delta t_{i,j} = \pm i\eta$). Both the
uniform orbital magnetization $M_{orb}$ and the anomalous Hall conductivity
$\sigma_{xy}$ are drastically suppressed by dilute impurities. The suppression ratio

$$ R = -\Delta M_{orb} / M_{orb}^0 $$

can exceed 50% with the introduction of 1% impurities. Unexpectedly, $R$ is
qualitatively insensitive to $\eta$, in high contrast to the naive expectation that
$R \propto \pi\xi_J^2$. The giant impurity effect originates from the nonlocal
contribution of the itinerant circulation of electrons.

## Model (Sec. II)

$$ H = \sum_{k,i,j,\sigma} h_{i,j}(k)\, c^\dagger_{k,i,\sigma} c_{k,j,\sigma}
      + \sum_{k,\sigma} I\, c^\dagger_{k,a,\sigma} c_{k,a,\sigma} $$

$t = -0.5$ eV (NN), $t' = -0.02$ eV (3rd-nearest intra-sublattice), $T = 0.01$ eV,
$n_{vHS} = 2.55$, $\mu = 0$, $I = 100$ eV, $N = 12 M_x M_y$ up to 1200, $N_k = 512^2$.

## Orbital magnetization (modern theory, Eq. 4)

$$ M_{orb} = \frac{1}{\pi N_k N} \sum_{n,k}\Big[ m_{n,k} f_{n,k}
   + \Omega_{n,k}\, T \ln\!\big(1 + e^{-(\epsilon_{n,k}-\mu)/T}\big) \Big] $$

with orbital moment $m_{n,k}$ and Berry curvature $\Omega_{n,k}$ built from the
interband velocity matrix elements $v^\mu_{n,l,k}$. First term = bulk, second = edge.
Without impurities $M_{orb} \propto \eta^3$ (triple-Q); with impurities the momentum
conservation is broken and $M_{orb} \propto \eta$ in the low-$\eta$ region.
